{
  "esm": "0.7.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "LANDFIRE_loader",
    "description": "Pure-I/O data loader for LANDFIRE (Landscape Fire and Resource Management Planning Tools) fire-behavior fuel-model classifications. Provides the Anderson 13 (FBFM13) or Scott & Burgan 40 (FBFM40) fuel-model code at ~30 m (~1 arc-second) resolution over the contiguous United States (CONUS), on a geographic (longlat/WGS84) lattice, sourced from the USGS LANDFIRE ImageServer REST API as a GeoTIFF cropped to the model domain.\n\nThis is the loader half of the landfire loader+regridding-model split (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §4.1/§7; bead esm-3nc.4). It is PURE I/O: it declares its source (url_template), the file variable it reads (with units), and its NATIVE grid expressed as a GDD Grid with a geographic (longlat/WGS84) crs descriptor. It performs NO reprojection and NO regridding — those are per-variable concerns of the regridding model (components/earthsci_data/landfire.esm), which references this file as a subsystem via {\"ref\": \"./landfire_loader.esm\"}.\n\nThe removed co-located blocks: the old DataLoaderSpatial block (proj4 crs string / grid_type / staggering / resolution) is replaced by the GDD `grid` (family + crs + dimensions + extents); the old per-loader `regridding` block (fill_value / extrapolation) is gone — regridding is declared per-variable on the model (landfire.esm `regrid`). This is a STATIC (time-invariant) dataset: there is NO `temporal` block, so the loader seeds CONST cadence (ess-v9a.5) — the runtime folds the field once at bind (kind: static; the GeoTIFF is fetched once per simulation domain and never refreshed). Cadence derives from the absence of `temporal`, orthogonal to the `kind` enum.\n\nMigrated from EarthSciData.jl@830435a065f27e99f10bba91107ca1730322cc6b:src/landfire.jl:246 (LANDFIREFileSet, LANDFIRE constructor). Split out of the pre-migration components/earthsci_data/landfire.esm (esm-19u5).",
    "tags": [
      "earthsci_data",
      "wildland_fire",
      "fuel_model",
      "landfire",
      "static",
      "data_loader",
      "pure-io",
      "conus",
      "longlat",
      "categorical"
    ],
    "created": "2026-06-25T00:00:00Z",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciData.jl contributors",
      "EarthSciModels migration (esm-3nc.4)"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "LANDFIRE (2022). LANDFIRE 2022 Fire Behavior Fuel Model (FBFM13/FBFM40). U.S. Department of Agriculture, Forest Service; U.S. Department of Interior. Available: https://landfire.gov/",
        "url": "https://landfire.gov/"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Anderson, H.E. (1982). Aids to determining fuel models for estimating fire behavior. USDA Forest Service, Intermountain Forest and Range Experiment Station. Gen. Tech. Rep. INT-122. — Source for Anderson 13 fuel model codes 1–13."
      },
      {
        "citation": "Scott, J.H. and Burgan, R.E. (2005). Standard fire behavior fuel models: a comprehensive set for use with Rothermel's surface fire spread model. USDA Forest Service Gen. Tech. Rep. RMRS-GTR-153. — Source for Scott & Burgan 40 fuel model codes (FBFM40 product)."
      },
      {
        "citation": "Source: EarthSciData.jl@830435a065f27e99f10bba91107ca1730322cc6b:src/landfire.jl (LANDFIREFileSet, LANDFIRE constructor). Test: test/landfire_test.jl. Docs: docs/src/landfire.md."
      }
    ]
  },
  "data_loaders": {
    "LANDFIRE": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "https://lfps.usgs.gov/arcgis/rest/services/Landfire_{version}/{version}_{product}_CONUS/ImageServer/exportImage?bbox={bbox_west_deg},{bbox_south_deg},{bbox_east_deg},{bbox_north_deg}&bboxSR=4326&imageSR=4326&size={image_width},{image_height}&format=tiff&pixelType=S16&interpolation=+RSP_NearestNeighbor&f=image"
      },
      "grid": {
        "family": "cartesian",
        "crs": {
          "projection": "longlat",
          "datum": "WGS84"
        },
        "description": "Native LANDFIRE grid: regular geographic (longlat/WGS84) lattice at ~30 m (~1 arc-second, 0.00027778°) resolution over CONUS. Geographic (unprojected) crs — the regridding model applies the longlat identity reprojection (ESD reprojection/longlat.esm, esd-47z.1). Migrated from the loader's former DataLoaderSpatial block (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §4.1); the loader describes this grid but performs no reprojection or regridding. The bounding box and cell counts are domain-derived at load time: the GeoTIFF is requested at the WGS84 envelope of the model domain (with a one-resolution-cell buffer), so lon/lat cell counts (n_lon, n_lat) are resolved from the source response at load time and clamped to the LANDFIRE ImageServer 4000×4000-pixel-per-request limit. The documented native cell size is 0.00027778° in both lon and lat; the data covers the contiguous United States.",
        "dimensions": [
          "lon",
          "lat"
        ],
        "extents": {
          "lon": {
            "n": "n_lon",
            "spacing": "uniform"
          },
          "lat": {
            "n": "n_lat",
            "spacing": "uniform"
          }
        },
        "parameters": {
          "n_lon": {
            "units": "1",
            "description": "Longitude cell count, resolved from the source GeoTIFF at load time. Domain-derived: image_width = min(4000, round((bbox_east_deg - bbox_west_deg) / 0.00027778))."
          },
          "n_lat": {
            "units": "1",
            "description": "Latitude cell count, resolved from the source GeoTIFF at load time. Domain-derived: image_height = min(4000, round((bbox_north_deg - bbox_south_deg) / 0.00027778))."
          }
        }
      },
      "variables": {
        "fuel_model": {
          "file_variable": "Band1",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Fire behavior fuel model code (categorical integer). Raw GeoTIFF pixel type S16; TiffImages reads as Q0f15 fixed-point — multiply by 32768 to recover integer fuel model codes. For FBFM13 (Anderson 13): codes 0 (no fuel), 1–13 (burnable), 91=urban, 92=snow/ice, 93=agriculture, 98=water, 99=barren. For FBFM40 (Scott & Burgan 40): codes 101–204 additional. Coverage: contiguous United States (CONUS) only. This is CATEGORICAL data — see metadata.interpolation_note and the regridding model's regrid.fuel_model description for the regridding-kernel consideration."
        }
      },
      "reference": {
        "citation": "USGS LANDFIRE (2022). LF2022 Fire Behavior Fuel Model 13 (FBFM13) / Fuel Model 40 (FBFM40). U.S. Department of Agriculture, Forest Service; U.S. Department of Interior.",
        "url": "https://landfire.gov/"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": ["wildland_fire", "fuel_model", "landfire", "static", "conus", "categorical", "longlat"],
        "earthscidata_source": "src/landfire.jl::LANDFIREFileSet",
        "api_type": "ArcGIS ImageServer REST (exportImage endpoint)",
        "file_format": "GeoTIFF, S16 signed 16-bit integer pixels (Q0f15 fixed-point in TiffImages; multiply by 32768 to get integer fuel model codes)",
        "native_resolution_deg": {
          "lon": 0.00027778,
          "lat": 0.00027778
        },
        "native_staggering": "Cell-centered (lon 'center', lat 'center') — LANDFIRE is a regular non-staggered raster. The regridding model regrids fuel_model conservatively per the migration spec (RFC §5.2; bead esm-3nc.4); see landfire.esm regrid.fuel_model and interpolation_note below for the categorical caveat.",
        "native_extent": {
          "comment": "Approximate CONUS envelope; the actual requested bbox is domain-derived at load time (WGS84 envelope of the model domain with a one-cell buffer).",
          "lon": [-125.0, -66.0],
          "lat": [24.0, 50.0]
        },
        "interpolation_note": "The upstream EarthSciData.jl loader regrids this CATEGORICAL dataset with nearest-neighbour (BSpline(Constant())) interpolation — interpolated values BETWEEN integer codes are physically meaningless. The new ESS RegridSpec offers only {conservative, bspline, cell_average}; per the esm-3nc.4 migration spec (cell-centered → conservative) the regridding model declares regrid.fuel_model.method = conservative. Downstream consumers (components/wildland_fire/fuel_model_lookup.esm and the fuel_* registered functions) round/clamp to integer codes via ifelse + interp.linear, tolerating non-integer inputs. This nearest-neighbour-vs-conservative consideration is carried forward as a documented gap (gotcha §8) pending a nearest/mode regrid kernel in ESS.",
        "bbox_computation": "The URL template substitutions {bbox_west_deg}, {bbox_south_deg}, {bbox_east_deg}, {bbox_north_deg}, {image_width}, {image_height} are domain-derived at runtime: the bounding box is the WGS84 envelope of the model domain (with a one-resolution-cell buffer), and the image dimensions are computed from the bbox extent divided by the requested resolution (default 1.0 arc-second ≈ 30m, clamped to 4000×4000 pixels per LANDFIRE ImageServer limit).",
        "url_substitutions": "{version}=LF2022 (default), {product}=FBFM13 (default, use FBFM40 for Scott & Burgan 40 models), {bbox_*_deg}=domain WGS84 bounding box in degrees, {image_width}/{image_height}=computed pixel dimensions",
        "url_defaults": {"version": "LF2022", "product": "FBFM13", "size_cap": 4000},
        "coverage": "Contiguous United States (CONUS) only. Requests outside CONUS may return fill values or errors.",
        "valid_products": ["FBFM13", "FBFM40"],
        "valid_versions": ["LF2020", "LF2022"],
        "cache_path_pattern": "landfire/{product}_{bbox_west}_{bbox_south}_{bbox_east}_{bbox_north}_{width}x{height}.tif",
        "static_note": "No temporal block: kind='static' and the absence of `temporal` seed CONST cadence (ess-v9a.5). The runtime fetches the GeoTIFF once per simulation domain and never reloads it (upstream DataFrequencyInfo uses a single interval spanning [starttime, endtime + 1 day], with build_interp_event firing once at simulation start)."
      }
    }
  }
}
